WEBVTT

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.680
The president of the United States has said that the need for maintaining civil defense

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.660
is one of the most serious problems confronting the nation today.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.400
Speaking on the importance of facing the facts with calmness and courage,

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.280
the president said,

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.270
The great chore you have here is to give people the facts, show them what they can do.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.580
get the federal leadership get the participation of the states and the municipalities without

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:41.720
terrifying i i have one great belief nobody in war or anywhere else ever made a good decision

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.640
if he was frightened to death you have to look back in the face but you have to have the stamina

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.640
to do it without uh just going uh starry

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:26.180
and sought rest, anything but the subject of our all-day conference.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.340
The question still obsessed me.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.060
I longed for sleep, but I could still hear their voices.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.620
How are we going to educate those people out there, Hammond?

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:47.030
How are we going to present to the American people the facts about possible panic and its prevention?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.420
Panic. Uncontrolled fear, according to the dictionary.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.540
Unreasoning action caused by the shock of a strange and threatening experience.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:02:59.960
But to millions of our citizens...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.680
it could have a far more important meaning.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.470
Because if our country is ever attacked,

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.910
mass panic could complicate the problem of recovery.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:29.970
Fear, the reaction of a child to a strange and...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.840
threatening experience.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:01.940
Thank you.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.360
Both of these people had reacted in a different way to minor distresses, petty annoyances.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.540
How would these same people react?

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.590
to a more shocking experience.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.880
What would each do?

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.280
in that most important moment or two following catastrophe.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:15.460
In my mind I recalled an incident that had recently taken place in my home.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:16.790
Oh

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.290
Children stood by the wilderness.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:31.770
But Mary reacted quickly.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:32.670
Automatic.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.570
Allaying the children's fears.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.180
Assigning duties.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.880
Providing leadership.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:48.180
In a jiffy, the fire was out.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.850
But what if my wife had not provided that kind of family leadership?

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:55.290
panic might have resulted.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.080
Thank you.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:05:58.720
Panic.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:05:59.980
That can start.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.640
with an individual and his fear.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.180
striking out in all directions with lightning speed.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.460
flaring into a great fire.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.420
Here we sit.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:12.490
possibly a cross-section of the people of America.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:16.970
But what would each of us do if disaster suddenly overtook us?

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:19.810
Some among us would succumb to fear.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.930
I recalled an incident one night at the movies.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.620
Ladies and gentlemen, please give me your attention.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.230
There is no need for alarm.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.580
A small fire is broken out backstage.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.540
And is being brought under control.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:52.530
In the meantime...

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.330
Please proceed to the exits.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.540
Now being opened by the ushers.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:57.530
I repeat.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:58.920
There's no need.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:06:59.970
Who are alarmed?

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:05.120
Another example of how people will react when given leadership.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:09.650
when information dispels the raw material of panic.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:10.980
You

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.210
boy and girl, probably high school kids.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.180
Drilled and re-drilled from the day they entered our schools in what to do.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:26.860
in the event of fire.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:30.000
I had read a report of it.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.760
school incident.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:33.500
Thank you.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.610
the resourcefulness of his class.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:39.330
The teacher had locked the exit usually used by the students.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.510
Immediately, one of the boys took over.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:53.010
instructed his fellow students to move at once to another exit.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.690
Here again was leadership.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:58.390
putting into effect a sound plan.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:00.000
Today,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.650
Today, fatalities caused by school fires are a rarity because of simple, well-practiced

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:06.090
plans.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:14.040
These are examples of people, young and old, taking charge, preventing panic.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.380
I thought of Greek disasters of the past.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:38.470
casually lists running into the thousand where panic could have increased the toll so easily

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:45.160
here were to be found many examples of people reacting intelligently leadership springing up

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:56.500
to take control people caring for the sick and injured proving once again that even untrained

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.720
people will not panic if given information

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:16.090
leadership a job to do yet the question was still in my mind how can we educate the people

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:24.360
of the united states against the dread psychological weapon of mass panic against rumors that can

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:29.810
spread like wildfire type of psychological warfare that a potential

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:37.980
enemy would use intruder radio broadcasts to disrupt civil defense to destroy faith in our

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:48.330
leaders rumors about our strength to retaliate leaflets to advance civil strife in short anything

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:53.600
to weaken our will to resist there will be no great reason for the existence of armies

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:59.180
they'll have undermined our enemies sufficiently before hostilities begin so that the military

00:09:59.180 --> 00:09:59.960
The organization...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.750
possess will be incapable of being used in the hour of need.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.060
We can be prepared against such warfare.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:15.720
Good leadership, sound planning, prompt information can very well be the means of conditioning

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:20.190
the behavior of our people, even in an age of hydrogen weapons.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:29.960
How would the people on this...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.200
The train reacts to an immediate danger.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:44.860
He's got loose from the train! I can see it up ahead!

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.820
We'll all be killed! Somebody do something!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:59.440
I couldn't warn you, folks!

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.560
We have to put this car on the siding for a bit.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.690
Automatic brakes will take hold in a minute.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:05.660
You'll feel them.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:29.970
It's a dream, but it gave...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:37.070
me the clue to the answer to my question in time of national emergency we'll need many more

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:43.970
conductors we can't depend on leaders springing up unexpectedly where will they come from will

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:52.130
he be a leader would she panic people are unpredictable without information leadership

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.840
and a job to do, they may panic.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.120
Pandemonium. Chaos. And there is my answer.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:16.500
Civil defense can make order out of chaos, can prevent panic from starting

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.620
by guiding the willing hands of survivors into organized activity.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:53.360
developing skilled leadership telling the public what is happening i saw these people

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:59.970
across section of the people of america and i long to cry out in the event

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:07.270
of enemy attack or major disaster you can be the one to prevent a chain reaction that could lead to

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:20.100
panic i felt the american people given the facts will understand the need and will act now to

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.980
preserve our nation
